# Cursor rules for Gaffa

Gaffa is a dynasty fantasy football platform for the Premier League, live at
gaffa.live.

**`AGENTS.md` is the operating contract.** Read it. It covers the definition of
done, what to ask before doing, writing style, the skills policy, and the free-tier
cost limits. This file does not restate those rules, so they cannot drift apart.

Deeper references, read when the task calls for them rather than up front:

- `docs/UI_RULES.md` — the binding UI rules. Read before any UI, CSS, or copy work.
- `DESIGN.md` — tokens, typography, mobile standards, banned patterns.
- `docs/DECISIONS.md` — what Duke actually decided. Check before asserting policy.
- `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md` — architecture, scoring engine, data pipeline.
- `docs/USER_GUIDE.md` — league mechanics and the reasoning behind them.

## Verification

`npm run build` must pass before you call work done or push. `npm test` and
`npm run check:ui` are safe to run unprompted.

## The one rule agents keep breaking

Headings and section titles are **title case** ("Record Book", "Title-Winning
XI"). Buttons are sentence case ("Submit proposal"), never uppercase.
`scripts/check-ui-rules.mjs` enforces this on write.
